WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:07.659
and Frank stood outside Grandpa's house.

2
00:00:07.679 --> 00:00:12.181
"Mom, I want to bring my sketch pad and crayons.

3
00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:16.002
I'm going to draw a picture of the lake," said Lisa.

4
00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:20.144
"I'm bringing my baseball and glove," said Frank.

5
00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:24.646
"Grandpa said he's going to show me how to throw a curve ball."

6
00:00:26.506 --> 00:00:27.827
"Okay, but hurry.

7
00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:30.368
Dad is waiting," said Mom.

8
00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:33.349
Dad was waiting at the lake with the boat.

9
00:00:33.369 --> 00:00:35.190
"Daddy! Daddy!

10
00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.891
I became a big girl today!"

11
00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:39.231
shouted Lisa.

12
00:00:39.251 --> 00:00:40.632
"A big girl?

13
00:00:41.012 --> 00:00:42.533
Really?" asked Dad.

14
00:00:42.553 --> 00:00:46.574
"Yes, I've got a loose tooth.

15
00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:49.215
See?" "Wow!"

16
00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:51.116
exclaimed Dad.

17
00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:52.597
"You are a big girl."

18
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:55.418
"See, see?

19
00:00:55.838 --> 00:00:57.639
Daddy, my tooth is out!"

20
00:00:58.159 --> 00:00:59.700
shouted Lisa excitedly.

21
00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:01.852
She held up her tooth.

22
00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:04.673
"What are you going to do with the tooth?"

23
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:05.873
asked Dad.

24
00:01:05.893 --> 00:01:13.335
"Tonight I am going to put it under my pillow and make a wish," replied Lisa.

25
00:01:13.356 --> 00:01:16.676
"Oh, I see," said Dad.

26
00:01:16.696 --> 00:01:18.957
"What are you going to wish for?"

27
00:01:18.977 --> 00:01:23.958
"I don't know yet," said Lisa, frowning.

28
00:01:23.978 --> 00:01:26.619
"I hadn't thought about it."

29
00:01:27.459 --> 00:01:29.720
Grandpa arrived with the life jackets.

30
00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:34.947
"When you do know," warned Grandpa, "you mustn't tell anyone.

31
00:01:35.307 --> 00:01:37.728
The tooth fairy only grants secret wishes."

32
00:01:37.748 --> 00:01:42.351
"Oh! Daddy, I can't tell you my wish.

33
00:01:42.851 --> 00:01:45.973
It's a secret," said Lisa seriously.

34
00:01:45.993 --> 00:01:48.874
"Are we going in the boat?"

35
00:01:49.435 --> 00:01:50.135
asked Frank.

36
00:01:50.155 --> 00:01:52.797
"Yes," said Dad.

37
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:55.698
"We are going to take the boat to the island."

38
00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:58.560
"To the island?

39
00:01:59.004 --> 00:02:00.945
Are there pirates on the island?"

40
00:02:01.505 --> 00:02:02.325
asked Lisa.

41
00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:05.626
"No," said Grandpa.

42
00:02:05.646 --> 00:02:10.807
"But a beautiful Native American princess once lived on the island."

43
00:02:12.588 --> 00:02:14.348
"Really?" asked Lisa.

44
00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:16.569
"What was her name?"

45
00:02:16.589 --> 00:02:19.530
"Her name was Sunapee.

46
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.271
The lake and the island are both named after her," answered Grandpa.

47
00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:26.992
"Why did she live on the island?"

48
00:02:27.432 --> 00:02:28.172
asked Frank.

49
00:02:29.388 --> 00:02:34.790
"She lived on the island because the man she loved died, and she didn't want to marry any

50
00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.930
other man," said Grandpa.

51
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.191
"Oh," said Lisa.

52
00:02:40.211 --> 00:02:42.952
"It must have been very lonely."

53
00:02:42.972 --> 00:02:47.493
"No, not lonely at all," answered Grandpa.

54
00:02:47.513 --> 00:02:52.895
"She was loved by all of the animals, especially the eagle king."

55
00:02:52.915 --> 00:02:56.556
"What happened to the princess?"

56
00:02:57.156 --> 00:02:57.896
asked Frank.

57
00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.501
"No one knows for sure," answered Grandpa.

58
00:03:03.422 --> 00:03:06.643
When everyone was in the boat, Grandpa told the story.

59
00:03:06.663 --> 00:03:11.485
"The eagle king loved the princess very much.

60
00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:13.186
He protected her from all men.

61
00:03:14.086 --> 00:03:19.368
Many men tried to go to the island to marry the princess, but the eagle king fought each

62
00:03:19.428 --> 00:03:19.749
of them.

63
00:03:21.809 --> 00:03:27.652
The Native Americans believe the princess married the eagle king because he was like her lost love."

64
00:03:29.196 --> 00:03:31.377
"Are there eagles on the island now?"

65
00:03:31.857 --> 00:03:32.638
asked Lisa.

66
00:03:32.658 --> 00:03:35.739
"Yes, many," answered Grandpa.

67
00:03:35.759 --> 00:03:38.200
"Will we see an eagle?"

68
00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.340
asked Frank.

69
00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.463
"Yes, you will see eagles," said Grandpa.

70
00:03:45.543 --> 00:03:48.344
Lisa and Frank both wanted to see the eagles.

71
00:03:49.845 --> 00:03:53.246
Lisa was so excited that she forgot about the tooth she was holding.

72
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.787
"Oh no!"

73
00:03:56.288 --> 00:03:57.148
cried Lisa.

74
00:03:58.248 --> 00:03:59.369
"My tooth is gone.

75
00:03:59.869 --> 00:04:02.431
I dropped it, and it fell into the lake.

76
00:04:02.931 --> 00:04:06.354
Now I have nothing to give to the tooth fairy."

77
00:04:06.374 --> 00:04:10.857
"There will be other teeth," said Grandpa.

78
00:04:10.877 --> 00:04:18.442
"Yes, but I had finally decided what I was going to wish for," whined Lisa.

79
00:04:18.462 --> 00:04:25.707
"As long as you don't tell anyone your wish, the tooth fairy will grant it to you next

80
00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:27.548
time," said Grandma.

81
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.701
"Look!" shouted Frank.

82
00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:34.142
"Is that an eagle?"

83
00:04:34.162 --> 00:04:40.526
"It's so high," said Lisa, forgetting about her lost tooth.

84
00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.928
"Watch it closely," said Grandpa.

85
00:04:44.948 --> 00:04:48.050
The eagle flew close by, flapping its wings.

86
00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.312
"Wow!" shouted everyone.

87
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:55.014
"Eagles are so fast!"

88
00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:56.475
exclaimed Frank.

89
00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.736
"A feather!"

90
00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.200
shouted Lisa.

91
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.221
"I caught a feather!"

92
00:05:03.821 --> 00:05:08.083
"Grandpa," asked Lisa, "do eagle feathers grow back?"

93
00:05:08.103 --> 00:05:12.584
"Yes. Yes, they do," said Grandpa slowly.

94
00:05:12.604 --> 00:05:15.645
"They grow back—just like baby teeth."

95
00:05:15.665 --> 00:05:21.927
"Do you think I can put this feather under my pillow and make a wish?"

96
00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:23.187
asked Lisa.

97
00:05:23.207 --> 00:05:26.748
"Hmm," said Grandpa.

98
00:05:27.956 --> 00:05:31.198
"That's an excellent question, but I don't know the answer.

99
00:05:31.758 --> 00:05:33.659
I don't know if there's a feather fairy.

100
00:05:34.279 --> 00:05:36.481
I've never tried making a wish on a feather."

101
00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:42.104
"Well, I'm going to make a wish on my eagle feather.

102
00:05:42.504 --> 00:05:45.786
Maybe Princess Sunapee will grant me my wish!"

103
00:05:46.206 --> 00:05:47.006
said Lisa.

104
00:05:47.026 --> 00:05:50.368
"Maybe she will," smiled Grandpa.

105
00:05:50.388 --> 00:05:57.492
"If there is a tooth fairy," said Lisa, "then there has to be a feather fairy.

106
00:05:57.908 --> 00:06:00.214
I'm sure that my wish will come true."
